  "decision_conditions": [
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposal would not have an unacceptable adverse impact on the levels of daylight received in habitable windows at Nos 118 and 120 Richmond Road. Furthermore, due to the siting, scale and the proposed separation distances, the proposal is likely to appear as an overbearing when viewed from the adjoining properties. The proposal, given the proposed separation distances and its siting, would result in an unacceptable loss of privacy and undue overlooking in relation to the property at No 120 Richmond Road. As such, the proposal is contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "It is considered that the collection of roof forms would not be in-keeping with the host dwelling and the surrounding area resulting in a jarring and incongruous appearance which would have an unacceptable impact on the existing street scene, conflicting with Paragraph 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policies D3 of the London Plan 2021, and Policy DM10 of the Council's Core Strategy 2012.\r",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that the proposal would not have an adverse impact on the existing car parking arrangement and would not lead to increased car parking pressures within the surrounding area that may lead to inconsiderate parking and therefore jeopardise highway safety. The proposal is therefore contrary to Paragraph 115 of the NPPF, 2024 and Policies DM9 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r"
  ],
